{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "8a9e2f7b-3c2e-4a1c-9b6e-001-swarm-native",
    "name": "OptimusDB • Swarm Off-Chain Credentials (Native UI Format)",
    "description": "Postman collection that accepts Swarmchestrate's *native* off-chain credential format exactly as produced in the UI (canonical core + keccak256 hash + EIP-191 signature).\n\nBase URL: `{{baseUrl}}`\n\n### Native (UI) Credential Shape\n```json\n{\n  \"@context\": [\"https://www.w3.org/2018/credentials/v1\"],\n  \"type\": [\"VerifiableCredential\"],\n  \"universeId\": \"<string>\",\n  \"issuerDID\": \"<string>\",\n  \"issuerAddress\": \"0x...\",\n  \"issuanceDate\": 1731191952,  // epoch seconds\n  \"expirationDate\": 1762811952, // epoch seconds\n  \"credentialSubject\": {\n    \"id\": \"0x<subject>\",\n    \"attributes\": [ {\"key\": \"RAM\", \"value\": \"16GB\"}, ... ]\n  },\n  \"hash\": \"0x...\",       // keccak256(JSON.stringify(canonical))\n  \"signature\": \"0x...\"   // personal_sign(hash)\n}\n```\n\n### New/Updated Endpoints\n- `POST /credentials/swarm` — store the native object as-is (plus server-side materialization)\n- `GET  /credentials/hash/:hash` — retrieve by credential content hash\n- `POST /credentials/verify-swarm` — verify native credential (structure + hash + signature + DB status)\n- `POST /credentials/revokeByHash` — revoke in DB using the content hash\n- `POST /credentials/query` — extended filters: `issuerAddress`, `universeId`, `swarmHash`, `chainId`, `status`, `limit`, `offset`\n\nAll endpoints remain idempotent where possible (same `hash` → same logical credential), so your UI can safely retry without creating duplicates.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "swarm-native"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0. Swarm Native (UI Canonical)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Store Swarm Credential (canonical + hash + signature)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Generate default times if not provided",
                  "const nowSec = Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000);",
                  "if (!pm.environment.get('swarmIssuanceSec')) pm.environment.set('swarmIssuanceSec', nowSec);",
                  "if (!pm.environment.get('swarmExpirationSec')) pm.environment.set('swarmExpirationSec', nowSec + (365 * 86400));",
                  "// placeholders for UI-provided values",
                  "if (!pm.environment.get('swarmUniverseId')) pm.environment.set('swarmUniverseId', '1');",
                  "if (!pm.environment.get('swarmIssuerDID')) pm.environment.set('swarmIssuerDID', '1');",
                  "if (!pm.environment.get('swarmIssuerAddress')) pm.environment.set('swarmIssuerAddress', '0x0000000000000000000000000000000000000000');",
                  "if (!pm.environment.get('swarmSubjectAddress')) pm.environment.set('swarmSubjectAddress', '0x0000000000000000000000000000000000000000');",
                  "// hash/signature must come from your UI; set placeholders if missing so request validates",
                  "if (!pm.environment.get('swarmHash')) pm.environment.set('swarmHash', '0xPLEASE_REPLACE_WITH_UI_HASH');",
                  "if (!pm.environment.get('swarmSignature')) pm.environment.set('swarmSignature', '0xPLEASE_REPLACE_WITH_UI_SIGNATURE');"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 201', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(201); });",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Response has success', function () { pm.expect(json.success).to.be.true; });",
                  "pm.test('Response returns a credentialId', function () { pm.expect(json.credentialId).to.exist; });",
                  "pm.environment.set('lastSwarmCredentialId', json.credentialId);",
                  "// keep the request hash/signature for subsequent steps",
                  "try {",
                  "  const req = JSON.parse(pm.request.body.raw);",
                  "  if (req.hash) pm.environment.set('lastSwarmHash', req.hash);",
                  "  if (req.signature) pm.environment.set('lastSwarmSignature', req.signature);",
                  "} catch (e) {}",
                  "if (json.ipfsHash) pm.environment.set('lastSwarmIpfsHash', json.ipfsHash);",
                  "console.log('✅ Stored swarm credential:', json.credentialId);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"@context\": [\"https://www.w3.org/2018/credentials/v1\"],\n  \"type\": [\"VerifiableCredential\"],\n  \"universeId\": \"{{swarmUniverseId}}\",\n  \"issuerDID\": \"{{swarmIssuerDID}}\",\n  \"issuerAddress\": \"{{swarmIssuerAddress}}\",\n  \"issuanceDate\": {{swarmIssuanceSec}},\n  \"expirationDate\": {{swarmExpirationSec}},\n  \"credentialSubject\": {\n    \"id\": \"{{swarmSubjectAddress}}\",\n    \"attributes\": [\n      { \"key\": \"role\", \"value\": \"Researcher\" },\n      { \"key\": \"clearance\", \"value\": \"L2\" }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"hash\": \"{{swarmHash}}\",\n  \"signature\": \"{{swarmSignature}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/credentials/swarm",
              "host": [ "{{baseUrl}}" ],
              "path": [ "credentials", "swarm" ]
            },
            "description": "Store a Swarm off-chain credential **exactly** as produced by the UI (canonical + `hash` + `signature`).\n\nServer-side SHOULD:\n- Persist the canonical core as-is for reproducible hashing\n- Idempotently upsert by `hash`\n- Optionally materialize W3C-like fields for indexing/query (issuer DID PKH, ISO dates, KV flattening)\n\nReturns: `{ success, credentialId, ipfsHash? }`"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Credential by Hash",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Contains credential', function () { pm.expect(json.credential).to.exist; });",
                  "pm.test('Round-trip canonical present', function () { pm.expect(json.credential['@context']).to.be.an('array'); });",
                  "console.log('📦 Retrieved by hash:', pm.environment.get('lastSwarmHash'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/credentials/hash/{{lastSwarmHash}}",
              "host": [ "{{baseUrl}}" ],
              "path": [ "credentials", "hash", "{{lastSwarmHash}}" ]
            },
            "description": "Retrieve a stored credential by its content `hash` (keccak256 over your canonical JSON)."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Verify Swarm Credential (native payload)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Verification result present', function () { pm.expect(json.verified).to.be.a('boolean'); });",
                  "if (!json.verified && json.errors) console.log('❌ Verification errors:', json.errors);",
                  "else console.log('✅ Verified');"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"@context\": [\"https://www.w3.org/2018/credentials/v1\"],\n  \"type\": [\"VerifiableCredential\"],\n  \"universeId\": \"{{swarmUniverseId}}\",\n  \"issuerDID\": \"{{swarmIssuerDID}}\",\n  \"issuerAddress\": \"{{swarmIssuerAddress}}\",\n  \"issuanceDate\": {{swarmIssuanceSec}},\n  \"expirationDate\": {{swarmExpirationSec}},\n  \"credentialSubject\": {\n    \"id\": \"{{swarmSubjectAddress}}\",\n    \"attributes\": [\n      { \"key\": \"role\", \"value\": \"Researcher\" },\n      { \"key\": \"clearance\", \"value\": \"L2\" }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"hash\": \"{{lastSwarmHash}}\",\n  \"signature\": \"{{lastSwarmSignature}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/credentials/verify-swarm",
              "host": [ "{{baseUrl}}" ],
              "path": [ "credentials", "verify-swarm" ]
            },
            "description": "Verify a **native** Swarm credential.\n\nServer SHOULD:\n1) Recompute `keccak256` over canonical core and compare to provided `hash`\n2) Optionally verify EIP‑191 personal_sign (`signature`) recovers `issuerAddress`\n3) Confirm DB status: exists, not revoked, not expired (and return reasons if not)\n\nReturns: `{ verified: boolean, errors?: string[], details?: {...} }`"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Revoke by Hash (DB mirror of on-chain revoke)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Revocation success', function () { pm.expect(json.success).to.be.true; });",
                  "console.log('🚫 Revoked in DB by hash:', pm.environment.get('lastSwarmHash'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"hash\": \"{{lastSwarmHash}}\",\n  \"universeId\": \"{{swarmUniverseId}}\",\n  \"issuerAddress\": \"{{swarmIssuerAddress}}\",\n  \"reason\": \"Revoked on-chain; mirrored in DB\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/credentials/revokeByHash",
              "host": [ "{{baseUrl}}" ],
              "path": [ "credentials", "revokeByHash" ]
            },
            "description": "Mark a credential **revoked** in DB using its `hash`.\n\nThis mirrors your on-chain `revokeOffChainCredential` event so DB queries match chain truth."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Query (extended: issuerAddress/universeId/swarmHash/chainId/status)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Has credentials array', () => pm.expect(json.credentials).to.be.an('array'));",
                  "console.log('🔎 Query returned:', json.count, 'items');"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"issuerAddress\": \"{{swarmIssuerAddress}}\",\n  \"universeId\": \"{{swarmUniverseId}}\",\n  \"chainId\": {{chainId}},\n  \"status\": \"active\",\n  \"limit\": 50,\n  \"offset\": 0\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/credentials/query",
              "host": [ "{{baseUrl}}" ],
              "path": [ "credentials", "query" ]
            },
            "description": "Query with Swarm-native filters. Supported filters (all optional):\n- `issuerAddress` (0x…)\n- `universeId` (string)\n- `swarmHash` (0x…)\n- `chainId` (number)\n- `status` (active | revoked | expired)\n- `limit`, `offset`"
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ],
      "description": "Endpoints that accept **exactly** the native Swarm UI credential format."
    },
    {
      "name": "1. Retrieve (generic by ID)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Get by Credential ID (DB-generated)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Credential present', () => pm.expect(json.credential).to.exist);",
                  "console.log('✅ Retrieved credential by ID');"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/credentials/get/{{lastSwarmCredentialId}}",
              "host": [ "{{baseUrl}}" ],
              "path": [ "credentials", "get", "{{lastSwarmCredentialId}}" ]
            },
            "description": "Retrieve the full stored credential by its DB `credentialId`."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ],
      "description": "Works with DB-generated identifiers in addition to hash-based access."
    },
    {
      "name": "2. Workflows (Swarm Native)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Workflow: Store → Get by Hash → Verify → Revoke → Verify (fails)",
          "item": [
            {
              "name": "Step 1 – Store (native)",
              "request": {
                "method": "POST",
                "header": [
                  { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
                ],
                "body": {
                  "mode": "raw",
                  "raw": "{\n  \"@context\": [\"https://www.w3.org/2018/credentials/v1\"],\n  \"type\": [\"VerifiableCredential\"],\n  \"universeId\": \"{{swarmUniverseId}}\",\n  \"issuerDID\": \"{{swarmIssuerDID}}\",\n  \"issuerAddress\": \"{{swarmIssuerAddress}}\",\n  \"issuanceDate\": {{swarmIssuanceSec}},\n  \"expirationDate\": {{swarmExpirationSec}},\n  \"credentialSubject\": {\n    \"id\": \"{{swarmSubjectAddress}}\",\n    \"attributes\": [\n      { \"key\": \"role\", \"value\": \"Researcher\" },\n      { \"key\": \"project\", \"value\": \"ICCS\" }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"hash\": \"{{swarmHash}}\",\n  \"signature\": \"{{swarmSignature}}\"\n}"
                },
                "url": {
                  "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/credentials/swarm",
                  "host": [ "{{baseUrl}}" ],
                  "path": [ "credentials", "swarm" ]
                }
              },
              "response": [],
              "event": [
                {
                  "listen": "test",
                  "script": {
                    "type": "text/javascript",
                    "exec": [
                      "pm.test('201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                      "const j = pm.response.json();",
                      "pm.environment.set('workflowSwarmCredentialId', j.credentialId);",
                      "pm.environment.set('workflowSwarmHash', pm.environment.get('swarmHash'));",
                      "console.log('✅ Step 1 stored:', j.credentialId);"
                    ]
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "Step 2 – Get by Hash",
              "request": {
                "method": "GET",
                "header": [],
                "url": {
                  "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/credentials/hash/{{workflowSwarmHash}}",
                  "host": [ "{{baseUrl}}" ],
                  "path": [ "credentials", "hash", "{{workflowSwarmHash}}" ]
                }
              },
              "response": [],
              "event": [
                {
                  "listen": "test",
                  "script": {
                    "type": "text/javascript",
                    "exec": [
                      "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                      "console.log('✅ Step 2 get by hash ok');"
                    ]
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "Step 3 – Verify (should pass)",
              "request": {
                "method": "POST",
                "header": [
                  { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
                ],
                "body": {
                  "mode": "raw",
                  "raw": "{\n  \"@context\": [\"https://www.w3.org/2018/credentials/v1\"],\n  \"type\": [\"VerifiableCredential\"],\n  \"universeId\": \"{{swarmUniverseId}}\",\n  \"issuerDID\": \"{{swarmIssuerDID}}\",\n  \"issuerAddress\": \"{{swarmIssuerAddress}}\",\n  \"issuanceDate\": {{swarmIssuanceSec}},\n  \"expirationDate\": {{swarmExpirationSec}},\n  \"credentialSubject\": {\n    \"id\": \"{{swarmSubjectAddress}}\",\n    \"attributes\": [\n      { \"key\": \"role\", \"value\": \"Researcher\" },\n      { \"key\": \"project\", \"value\": \"ICCS\" }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"hash\": \"{{workflowSwarmHash}}\",\n  \"signature\": \"{{swarmSignature}}\"\n}"
                },
                "url": {
                  "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/credentials/verify-swarm",
                  "host": [ "{{baseUrl}}" ],
                  "path": [ "credentials", "verify-swarm" ]
                }
              },
              "response": [],
              "event": [
                {
                  "listen": "test",
                  "script": {
                    "type": "text/javascript",
                    "exec": [
                      "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                      "const j = pm.response.json();",
                      "pm.test('verified true', () => pm.expect(j.verified).to.be.true);",
                      "console.log('✅ Step 3 verified ok');"
                    ]
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "Step 4 – Revoke by Hash",
              "request": {
                "method": "POST",
                "header": [
                  { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
                ],
                "body": {
                  "mode": "raw",
                  "raw": "{\n  \"hash\": \"{{workflowSwarmHash}}\",\n  \"universeId\": \"{{swarmUniverseId}}\",\n  \"issuerAddress\": \"{{swarmIssuerAddress}}\",\n  \"reason\": \"Contract revoke mirrored\"\n}"
                },
                "url": {
                  "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/credentials/revokeByHash",
                  "host": [ "{{baseUrl}}" ],
                  "path": [ "credentials", "revokeByHash" ]
                }
              },
              "response": [],
              "event": [
                {
                  "listen": "test",
                  "script": {
                    "type": "text/javascript",
                    "exec": [
                      "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                      "const j = pm.response.json();",
                      "pm.test('revoked', () => pm.expect(j.success).to.be.true);",
                      "console.log('🚫 Step 4 revoked by hash');"
                    ]
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "Step 5 – Verify again (should fail due to revocation)",
              "request": {
                "method": "POST",
                "header": [
                  { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
                ],
                "body": {
                  "mode": "raw",
                  "raw": "{\n  \"@context\": [\"https://www.w3.org/2018/credentials/v1\"],\n  \"type\": [\"VerifiableCredential\"],\n  \"universeId\": \"{{swarmUniverseId}}\",\n  \"issuerDID\": \"{{swarmIssuerDID}}\",\n  \"issuerAddress\": \"{{swarmIssuerAddress}}\",\n  \"issuanceDate\": {{swarmIssuanceSec}},\n  \"expirationDate\": {{swarmExpirationSec}},\n  \"credentialSubject\": {\n    \"id\": \"{{swarmSubjectAddress}}\",\n    \"attributes\": [\n      { \"key\": \"role\", \"value\": \"Researcher\" },\n      { \"key\": \"project\", \"value\": \"ICCS\" }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"hash\": \"{{workflowSwarmHash}}\",\n  \"signature\": \"{{swarmSignature}}\"\n}"
                },
                "url": {
                  "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/credentials/verify-swarm",
                  "host": [ "{{baseUrl}}" ],
                  "path": [ "credentials", "verify-swarm" ]
                }
              },
              "response": [],
              "event": [
                {
                  "listen": "test",
                  "script": {
                    "type": "text/javascript",
                    "exec": [
                      "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                      "const j = pm.response.json();",
                      "pm.test('verified false', () => pm.expect(j.verified).to.be.false);",
                      "pm.test('has revocation error', () => pm.expect((j.errors || []).join(' ')).to.match(/revok/i));",
                      "console.log('✅ Step 5 fails verification as expected');"
                    ]
                  }
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "description": "End-to-end using the **native UI payload** and hash-centric endpoints."
        }
      ],
      "description": "Swarm-native workflows"
    }
  ],
